# Custom units (API.md §2.1, PROJECT §5.6). Sign in first with dev-login (Development only).
# For the admin call sign in with an email listed in Admin__Emails__0. Task U1 uses database recipes_u1.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5101/api/v1
@productId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@unitId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Sign in (dev-login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "email": "anna@test.local", "nickname": "anna" }

### Units for every product, plus the units of one product (product units first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/units?productId={{productId}}

### Search by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/units?q=fili&limit=10

### A unit for one product: 1 puszka = 400 g (201, or 200 with the existing unit)
POST {{baseUrl}}/units
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "name": "puszka", "forms": { "one": "puszka", "few": "puszki", "many": "puszek", "fraction": "puszki" }, "productId": "{{productId}}", "equals": { "value": 400, "unit": "g" } }

### A unit for every product: 1 filiżanka = 150 ml
POST {{baseUrl}}/units
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "name": "filiżanka", "forms": { "one": "filiżanka", "few": "filiżanki", "many": "filiżanek", "fraction": "filiżanki" }, "productId": null, "equals": { "value": 150, "unit": "ml" } }

### Edit a unit (admin; the amount only while nothing uses it, 400 unit.in_use otherwise)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/units/{{unitId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "name": "puszka", "forms": { "one": "puszka", "few": "puszki", "many": "puszek", "fraction": "puszki" }, "productId": "{{productId}}", "equals": { "value": 425, "unit": "g" } }
